Just days after the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-homeview/">HomeView</a>'s launch, some owners are reporting problems with Siri, timers, and music playback on Apple's new smart home hub, based on multiple <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494413/"><em>MacRumors</em> forum</a> <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494370/">threads</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homeview_home_screen_feature-1.jpg" alt="" width="2071" height="1165" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071442" /><br/>
In the <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494413/">longest discussion</a>, which now spans over one hundred posts, several people say their HomeView refuses to set timers or alarms, and instead claims that a software update is required – even though the device reports that it is up to date. In <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494370/">another thread</a>, one poster said an AppleCare senior advisor told them other owners had reported the same problem, and that cold-rebooting their paired iPhone cleared it.<br/>
<br/>
Other owners describe Siri taking minutes to respond or repeatedly announcing that it is "downloading Siri." Elsewhere, in two <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494362/">separate</a> <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/2494405/">threads</a>, owners report music commands failing outright or being carried out on their iPhone instead of the HomeView, even when the device shows Siri listening on screen. That's not all, either. Some owners with multiple units say commands meant for one room play in another, for no apparent reason.<br/>
<br/>
Let's not overstate the case, though. Not everyone is seeing problems with HomeView. Several people have reported their units working as expected, and some say that any issues cleared after rebooting the HomeView, their iPhone, or both. <br/>
<br/>
Apple has already said a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/12/apple-plans-homeview-update-with-siri-fix/">software update coming next month</a> will fix a separate issue in which Siri AI claims not to have a camera and won't let recognized users unlock doors and garages by voice. Apple already released a software update that addresses <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/149851">several vulnerabilities</a>, including issues with AirPlay, Messages, and Bluetooth.<br/>
<br/>
